\f0\fs24
\pard\qc\b\fs36\cf1 Worst Cell Identification Logic\cf0\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa240\par
\pard\b\fs28\cf1 Objective\cf0\b0\fs24\par
\pard Worst cells are identified based on combined radio performance, not a single KPI. The goal is to find cells that show poor health across multiple important radio KPIs.\par
\pard\sa200\par
\pard\b\fs28\cf1 KPI Groups Used\cf0\b0\fs24\par
\trowd\trgaph108\trleft0\cellx3600\cellx8200
\intbl\b KPI Group\b0\cell\b Bad Condition\b0\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph108\trleft0\cellx3600\cellx8200
\intbl Load / PRB\cell High value is bad\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph108\trleft0\cellx3600\cellx8200
\intbl Throughput\cell Low value is bad\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph108\trleft0\cellx3600\cellx8200
\intbl Accessibility\cell Low value is bad\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph108\trleft0\cellx3600\cellx8200
\intbl Availability\cell Low value is bad\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph108\trleft0\cellx3600\cellx8200
\intbl Radio Quality\cell Low value is bad\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph108\trleft0\cellx3600\cellx8200
\intbl Retainability / Drops\cell High value is bad\cell\row
\pard\sa200\par
\pard\b\fs28\cf1 Example KPI Mapping\cf0\b0\fs24\par
\trowd\trgaph108\trleft0\cellx4300\cellx8500
\intbl\b Uploaded KPI Example\b0\cell\b KPI Group\b0\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph108\trleft0\cellx4300\cellx8500
\intbl PRB DL Utilization\cell Load / PRB\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph108\trleft0\cellx4300\cellx8500
\intbl User DL Throughput\cell Throughput\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph108\trleft0\cellx4300\cellx8500
\intbl RRC Success Rate\cell Accessibility\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph108\trleft0\cellx4300\cellx8500
\intbl Cell Availability\cell Availability\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph108\trleft0\cellx4300\cellx8500
\intbl CQI / SINR / RSRP / RSRQ\cell Radio Quality\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph108\trleft0\cellx4300\cellx8500
\intbl Drop Rate / DCR / Packet Loss\cell Retainability / Drops\cell\row
\pard\sa200\par
\pard\b\fs28\cf1 Evaluation Process\cf0\b0\fs24\par
\pard 1. Read all KPI records from the selected KPI upload.\par
\pard 2. Automatically identify KPI columns that match the radio KPI groups.\par
\pard 3. Evaluate each cell across the selected KPI groups.\par
\pard 4. Compare KPI direction: high-is-bad KPIs increase badness when values are high, and low-is-bad KPIs increase badness when values are low.\par
\pard 5. Check threshold rules and assign severity: CRITICAL, MAJOR, MINOR, WARNING, or NORMAL.\par
\pard 6. Give each KPI a badness score using file comparison and threshold severity.\par
\pard 7. Combine KPI scores for each cell.\par
\pard 8. Add extra penalty when a cell has problems in multiple KPI groups.\par
\pard 9. Sort cells by total combined badness score.\par
\pard\sa200\par
\pard\b\fs28\cf1 Final Ranking\cf0\b0\fs24\par
\pard The final worst-cell rank is based on the combined badness score across multiple radio KPIs. A cell with multiple KPI issues ranks worse than a cell with only one KPI issue.\par
\pard\sa200\par
\pard\b\fs28\cf1 Example\cf0\b0\fs24\par
\pard Cell A has high PRB, low throughput, poor CQI, and low availability. Cell B has only high PRB. Cell A ranks worse because its overall radio health is degraded across multiple KPI groups.\par
\pard\sa200\par
\pard\b\fs28\cf1 Conclusion\cf0\b0\fs24\par
\pard\b Worst Cell = cell with the highest combined radio KPI degradation.\b0\par
\pard This follows standard RF practice, where 4-5 key KPIs are reviewed together before identifying worst cells.\par
}
